   "evidence": "In the proof, `toRelativeCWComplex C`, `range_eq_empty`, and `RelCWComplex.toCWComplex univ` don't use finiteness. Only `RelCWComplex.finite_cells_of_finite` and `finite_of_finite_cells` do. `CWType.exists_homotopyEquiv` (Classical/CWType.lean:40) has the same shape without finiteness.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/CWComplex/Comparison.lean",
   "fix": "Define the CW structure on `univ : Set C` for any `[CWComplex C]` (a def or an existential without `Finite`). Prove `RelCWComplex.Finite (univ : Set C)` from `[RelCWComplex.Finite C]` as a separate lemma or instance, and derive `FiniteCWType.exists_homotopyEquiv_univ` from those two.",
   "issue": "`exists_cwComplex_univ` assumes `[RelCWComplex.Finite C]` for its whole conclusion and hides the CW structure in an existential. The structure `(toRelativeCWComplex C).toRelCWComplex` \u2192 `RelCWComplex.toCWComplex univ` exists for every CW complex `C`; finiteness is only used for the `RelCWComplex.Finite` half. This also blocks the `CWType` analogue of `exists_homotopyEquiv_univ`.",
   "line": 193
  }
